# Next bounded task43 preparation

This is a brief for future work, not authorization from this artifact to run
an intervention. Preserve the active baseline/residual/class-balanced/prior
matrix and its round-robin trajectory. The two archived terminal checkpoints
are separate historical frozen-weight diagnostics, not sustained-study resumes.

1. Bind each original checkpoint and source/runtime to the 16 manifest frames,
   physical observation lineage, V3 decoder and full 1,279 native GT. Use the
   checkpoint/manifest/receipt pins in [archived-evidence.json](archived-evidence.json).
   Recover the relevant task42 object/proposal identities before interpreting
   per-object changes. Pin labels for scoring without allowing them into
   calibration inputs.
2. Specify a control with every module in evaluation mode and unchanged saved
   buffers. Specify the per-frame batch-statistics arm separately: freeze all
   parameters; set only the identified pillar BN to current-statistics mode;
   keep every other module's declared mode. Preserve the original padding
   population and epsilon. Snapshot all buffers, every mode flag and RNG before
   each frame, restore them afterward and verify bitwise equality. Make zero
   optimizer calls. Refuse unexplained state or parameter changes.
3. First implement a literal CPU live Insula normalization/state checker for
   axes, padding, moments and restoration. Then prepare independently reviewable
   unchanged-weight head export and official native replay for the original
   and per-frame arms. A training-only recalibration arm remains conditional
   until pass order/count, momentum, counter rules and its allowed observation
   set are frozen explicitly. Do not silently replace original buffers.
4. Report per-frame/class loss, proposals, ranking/survival, geometry/heading and
   native AP/APH on identical V3/full-GT inputs. Lower loss alone cannot answer
   whether normalization state hides native learning. Preserve all original
   states and obtain required HDFS readback/live recovery before local release.

The present evidence supplies model names, buffer keys/hashes, checkpoint
availability and historical gaps. It supplies no changed-buffer native outcome,
recalibration recipe or complete diagnostic state closure. Keep43 open until
its own independent execution and quality evidence are admitted; a single
frozen checkpoint cannot satisfy the two-sample sustained fitting gate.
